{{define "job-help-trigger" -}}
<button
    type="button"
    class="info-trigger"
    aria-label="When to run {{.}}"
    aria-haspopup="dialog"
    up-follow
    up-layer="new popup"
    up-content="#job-help-{{.}}"
    up-class="info-popup"
    up-position="bottom"
    up-align="left"
    up-history="false"
    up-dismissible="key outside"
><span aria-hidden="true">[?]</span></button>
{{- end}}

{{define "scan-job-help"}}
    <template id="job-help-scan">
        <section class="job-help" aria-labelledby="job-help-scan-title">
            <h2 id="job-help-scan-title">When to run Scan</h2>
            <p>Refresh how your music is organized using information already saved in your library. Your music files are not read or downloaded again.</p>
            <ul>
                <li>After saving changes to Artist Split Rules.</li>
                <li>After changing how artist names, genres, or styles are grouped or recognized through these configuration settings:
                    <ul>
                        <li><code>scan.album_artist_split_tokens</code></li>
                        <li><code>scan.primary_genre_split_tokens</code></li>
                        <li><code>scan.secondary_genre_split_tokens</code></li>
                        <li><code>scan.genre_style_aliases</code></li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li>After a new taxonomy version has loaded successfully, as shown in the startup logs.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="job-help-note"><strong>Changed your music files?</strong> Use Sync instead—for example, if you added songs or edited their tags. Sync also applies your latest organization rules, so there is no need to run both.</p>
        </section>
    </template>
{{end}}

{{define "sync-job-help"}}
    <template id="job-help-sync">
        <section class="job-help" aria-labelledby="job-help-sync-title">
            <h2 id="job-help-sync-title">When to run Sync</h2>
            <p>Read your files again and rebuild the library, reusing cached resources. Remote files are downloaded again.</p>
            <ul>
                <li>After adding, modifying, renaming, moving, or deleting audio files, including changes to their tags.</li>
                <li>After changing roots in your configuration. Root changes also queue a sync at startup.</li>
                <li>After adding, modifying, renaming, moving, or deleting sidecar files, such as cover images.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="job-help-note"><strong>One job is enough:</strong> Sync includes the library rebuild performed by Scan. When both are needed, queue only Sync.</p>
        </section>
    </template>
{{end}}

{{define "reset-job-help"}}
    <template id="job-help-reset">
        <section class="job-help" aria-labelledby="job-help-reset-title">
            <h2 id="job-help-reset-title">When to run Reset</h2>
            <p>Start over when you want to discard saved artist split decisions and cached resources, then build a fresh library from your files.</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Clears library records, artist split rules, artwork caches, and other jobs and logs.</li>
                <li>Runs a full Sync, recreating split mappings and fetching resources as needed.</li>
                <li>Keeps the taxonomy, instance identity, and the running reset job. Your source music files are unchanged.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>For ordinary file or configuration changes, use Scan or Sync.</p>
            <p class="job-help-note"><strong>Bookmarks will break:</strong> Rebuilt library records receive new IDs. Bookmarks to old records will return “not found” (404), as intended after a reset.</p>
        </section>
    </template>
{{end}}
